The Compact Modal Matrix: 5 Positions to Rule Them All
If we throw out brute-force tracking of all 288 raw spark points and rely on our Chladni-plate modal interference model, we don't need a massive array. To fully describe any elementary particle known to modern physics (stripping away speculative WIMPs and gravitons), we only need a 5-position modal descriptor vector (M_5):
